# Context

## Background
Run autoresearch-ar1-001 tested the seven permitted rule knobs of the
V0.8 succession game around the fee-1 incumbent, one change per cycle,
with paired screens, fresh holdouts, and a preregistered
counterplay-availability veto (tools/contest_audit.py). The fee-2
diagnostic confirmed the veto was needed: the old mechanical checks
alone still promote the known-bad fee-2 variant.

## Why This Way
V0.8 is kept unchanged because every tested direction failed a
preregistered gate or the live check. The only offline survivor
(challenge_bonus 2 to 1) passed all offline gates and a 384-game
paired confirmation (cancellations -22.2%), but was rejected by the
authorized live Decisions comparison: live players bought the +1
boost 0 of 3 times (14% at +2), unboosted contests beat a full-set
claimant only 43% (82% at +2), and the first challenger won 4 of 4
finished games. The offline gain was an artifact of scripted bots
auto-purchasing the boost.

## Gotchas
- Bot-calibrated counterplay floors do not transfer to live play:
  live response purses sit at zero Prestige on 53-68% of turns.
- Compare win shares only within paired same-seed suites; across-seed
  96-game shares swing about 10 points (see the cycle-1 amendment).
- cycles/01/verdict-amendment.json documents an analyst error and its
  correction; the driver's paired checks were right all along.

